[[File:Rock-climbing boots detail.png|left|100px]]
'''Rock-climbing boots''' are an [[unobtainable item]] released along with the [[Grand Exchange]] as a joke. It is impossible to actually buy it, because the item only appears when searching the Grand Exchange, and is not an item that can actually be obtained.
{{Clear|left}}

[[File:Monkey (Monkey Madness I) detail.png|left|150x150px]]
}}
The '''monkey''' is a talkative animal obtained during the [[Monkey Madness I]] quest. Unlike other animals in-game, it stays in your inventory rather than following you around. 

Using any form of teleportation will cause the monkey to vanish. The monkey cannot be banked.

If you drop the monkey, it wanders around for about 30 seconds before disappearing, during which time it can be picked up again by talking to it. However, if the monkey is dropped on [[Karamja]], it becomes a [[monster]] like other Karamjan monkeys and exclaims "Yay! I'm free!," granting the player [[Thieving]] experience equal to twice their level before disappearing.

While in your inventory, the monkey can be poked, much to its annoyance, and it will often interrupt the player with forced dialogue. It can be fed [[banana]]s, [[monkey nuts]], [[monkey bar]]s, and [[banana stew]], although it will claim to not want the latter items, despite eating them anyway. The monkey will also occasionally eat bananas in your inventory without notice.

[[File:Antique lamp (One Small Favour) detail.png|left|180px]]
The '''antique lamp''' is an item obtained from [[Yanni Salika]] after completing the [[One Small Favour]] [[quest]]. Two are given to the player, and each lamp grants 10,000 [[experience]] in a [[skill]] of the player's choosing, given that the skill is over level 30. The lamp cannot be banked, but either of the two lamps can be reclaimed if dropped, even if the other of the two was used.

Even though the lamp can be dropped instead of being destroyed, and many can be dropped to the ground, extras cannot be obtained with the [[drop trick]], as the player may only hold a maximum of two before using the first lamp, and then a maximum of one until using the second lamp, whereupon no further lamps can be picked back up.

'''Note:''' the One Small Favour quest will not '''really''' be considered completed, being shown in yellow in the quest log and stopping the player from being able to start [[King's Ransom]] and [[Swan Song]], until both antique lamps are used. This happens even if the lamps are dropped in order to be retrieved later from Yanni Salika. Whether this is by design or is a bug is unclear.

{{One Small Favour}}
{{Experience lamp}}

