The '''hand mirror''' is a quest item used in the [[Mourning's End Part II]] and the [[Song of the Elves]] quest. It is obtained by pulling a lever in the [[Temple of Light]] near the start of the quest and is needed to solve the light puzzle in the Temple. As the player progresses through the puzzle they are rewarded with more mirrors in order to unlock more complicated parts of the puzzle. The mirrors redirect light to the place it needs to go if you put it at the right angle.

[[File:Blue flowers (Trouble Brewing) detail.png|left|150px]]
'''Blue flowers''' are an item obtained within the [[Trouble Brewing]] [[minigame]]. Blue flowers and [[red flowers (Trouble Brewing)|red flowers]] are found in the minigame outside the opposite team's base. Team members must collect their team's coloured flowers and place them in the [[kettle (Trouble Brewing)|kettle]] in order to make their team's [[Bowl of blue water|coloured water]] which is then used as an ingredient in the [[rum (blue)|rum]]. 

Players can only carry 5 flowers at a time, attempting to gather more will yield the message: {{mes|You have plenty of those.}}

These flowers cannot be taken out of the minigame but are tradeable within, and have a trade value of 1 coin. This item cannot be picked up using [[Telekinetic Grab]], attempting to do so will yield the message: {{mes|I can't use Telekinetic Grab on this object.}}

[[File:Red flowers (Trouble Brewing) detail.png|left|150px]]
'''Red flowers''' are an item obtained within the [[Trouble Brewing]] [[minigame]]. Red flowers and [[blue flowers (Trouble Brewing)|blue flowers]] are found in the minigame outside the opposite team's base. Team members must collect their team's coloured flowers and place them in the [[Kettle (Trouble Brewing)|kettle]] in order to make their team's [[Bowl of red water|coloured water]] which is then used as an ingredient in the [[Rum (blue)|rum]].

Players can only carry 5 flowers at a time, attempting to gather more will yield the message: {{mes|You have plenty of those.}}

These flowers cannot be taken out of the minigame but are tradeable within, and have a trade value of 1 coin. This item cannot be picked up using [[Telekinetic Grab]], attempting to do so will yield the message: {{mes|I can't use Telekinetic Grab on this object.}}

[[File:Monkey (Trouble Brewing) detail.png|left|130px]]
}}
A '''monkey''' is used in [[Trouble Brewing]] to gather [[bitternut]]s. They are found in the island in between the two bases, and they can be caught awarding the player with 15 [[Agility]] and [[Hunter]] experience. To use it to obtain bitternuts, a [[bowl of red water]] or a [[bowl of blue water]] must be used on the monkey, making it a [[red monkey]] or a [[blue monkey]]. The dyed monkey can then be used on a [[Bitternut Tree]], and it will throw down a bitternut to the player after some time if the player is within range of the tree. If a monkey from the opposing team is in the tree as well, the two monkeys will fight, only one will throw down a bitternut, and the other will disappear.

With completion of [[Monkey Madness II]] or a [[m'speak amulet]], the player can "Anger the monkey" or "Caution the monkey" when talking to it. An angry monkey will grab the nut quickly, but will always lose a fight if there is one. A cautious monkey will take longer to grab the nut, but will always win the fight. A player can have a maximum of two monkeys, and a team can have a maximum of twelve. If the player chooses to release the monkey, a level 1 Monkey will spawn.

[[File:Blue monkey detail.png|left|130px]]
}}
