[[File:Broken charm detail.png|130px|left]]

A '''broken charm''' is sent to the player's [[grave]] if a charm is in their inventory when killed by another player in [[Deadman Mode]]. The killer receives [[coins]]. This item serves no purpose.

{{Deadman Mode}}

[[File:Trinket dust detail.png|130px|left]]
'''Trinket dust''' is the remains of [[Deadman Mode]] [[Trinket (disambiguation)|trinkets]] upon player death.

{{Deadman Mode}}

[[File:Carrot juice glass detail.png|130px|left]]
The '''carrot juice glass''' was a special drinking glass given to the player by [[Wheeler]] during the [[2025 Easter event]]. Despite its similarities to a standard [[beer glass]], Wheeler insisted it is specifically made for holding carrot juice and [[fancy carrot juice]].

{{2025 Easter event}}

[[File:Rotten turnip detail.png|100px|left]]
The '''rotten turnip''' is an item similar to the [[rotten potato]] that is used to assist with developing plugins. It is not currently accessible and is only known to exist in the [[cache]].

{{Jagex Moderator Items}}

[[File:Mind mender detail.png|130px|left]]
The '''mind mender''' is an [[unobtainable item]] released with the third part of [[Varlamore]]. Judging from its config name (<code>aec_mind_mender</code>), it is believed to be part of [[An Existential Crisis]], an unreleased quest.

{{Unobtainable items}}

[[File:Key (Forebearer Janus) detail.png|left|100px]]
A '''key''' is found upon interrogating [[Forebearer Janus]] during the quest, [[The Final Dawn]]. This key is used to unlock the trapdoor, located south-west inside his house.

{{The Final Dawn}}
{{Keys}}

[[File:Canvas piece detail.png|130px|left]]
The '''canvas piece''' is an item obtained during [[The Final Dawn]], in which players must find a [[Key (The Final Dawn)|key]] inside the drawers within [[Metzli, Teokan of Ranul|Augur Metzli's]] chambers to unlock the chest that holds the canvas piece. After receiving the canvas piece, players must use it on the sun and moon mural to unlock a hidden room.

{{The Final Dawn}}

[[File:Key (The Final Dawn) detail.png|left|100px]]
A '''key''' is obtained during [[The Final Dawn]] by searching the drawers in backroom of the [[Twilight Temple]] basement, past the [[Emissary Enforcer]]. This key is used to unlock the nearby drawer that contains a [[canvas piece]].

{{The Final Dawn}}
{{Keys}}

[[File:Antique lamp (The Final Dawn) detail.png|130px|left]]
The '''antique lamp''' is a reward from [[The Final Dawn]] quest. The lamp grants 55,000 experience to any combat skill, including [[Prayer]]. You must have at least level 40 in the skill you wish to gain experience in.

The lamp cannot be banked. However, if the player prefers to use it at a later date, it can be destroyed and reclaimed from [[Prince Itzla]] whenever the player wishes to do so.

{{The Final Dawn}}
{{Experience lamp}}

[[File:Keystone fragment detail.png|130px|left]]
A '''keystone fragment''' is an item given to the player by [[Eyatlalli]] during [[The Final Dawn]]. It acts as a connection to the prototype version of the [[Monolith (Neypotzli)|icosahedron]] found in a hidden room within [[Neypotzli]], in which the player uses it as a guide to locate its entrance.

{{The Final Dawn}}

[[File:Knife blade detail.png|130px|left]]
A '''knife blade''' is obtained within the ruins beneath the [[Crypt of Tonali]] during [[The Final Dawn]], found by searching old tools in the moon puzzle room area. They are used to obtain [[ancient roots]] and cutting them into [[root kindling]], which are used to complete the puzzle.

{{The Final Dawn}}

