[[File:Token (Final Dawn) detail.png|130px|left]]
The purple '''token''' can be obtained by completing a specific task in [[Varlamore]] centred around the [[Capybara#Picnic|capybara]] and [[Pygmy hippo calf#Picnic|pygmy hippo calf]] picnic located south-west of [[Kastori]]. According to [[Cobado]], this token, alongside the seven [[Token (Varlamore)|red tokens]] and four [[nasty token]]s, were hidden by the capybaras of Varlamore as a test to see how far someone would go in collecting them all.{{CiteNPC|npc=Cobado|quote=Cobado: The tokens! It's always been about the tokens! The capybaras left them for us, to test if we were worthy! Now you finally have them all!<br>Player: Okay... But what do I do with them all now?<br>Cobado: Do with them? Well... nothing. You've already passed the test!<br>Player: So there isn't some big reward?<br>Cobado: Reward? Of course not! That was part of the test! They wanted to see how far you'd go!}}

If a player performs a [[Jig]] at the picnic, the animals will judge the player's dance moves depending on four conditions:
{{List|c=1|
* Playing the [[Country Jig]] music track
* Wearing the [[orange (hat)|orange hat]]
* Dropping [[Humphrey Dumphrey]] from the quest [[Scrambled!]] on the opposite side of the picnic
* Having four [[metztonalli white]]s in the inventory.
}}
If all four conditions are met, the capybara will give the player the purple token. The purple token can be taken to [[Cobado]] while wearing [[Orange (hat)|an orange]] as a hat along with all 7 [[token (Varlamore)|red tokens]] and all 4 [[nasty token]]s to receive a [[blueberry muffin]] and 100,000 [[coins]]. If the player has the purple token, but not the rest of the tokens, Cobado will give the player 1 coin and tells them to find the rest if they have not yet received the blueberry muffin.

{{Map|1265,3003|mtype=pin||caption=[[Picnic]] location.|align=left}}

